WEBVTT

00:01.635 --> 00:04.603
♪ it seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.605 --> 00:07.773
♪ is violence in movies
and sex on tv ♪

00:07.775 --> 00:11.510
♪ but where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.512 --> 00:14.513
♪ on which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.515 --> 00:17.916
♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.918 --> 00:21.420
♪ lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.422 --> 00:23.021
♪ all the things that make us ♪

00:23.023 --> 00:24.356
♪ laugh and cry ♪

00:24.358 --> 00:30.362
♪ he's... A...
Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.635 --> 00:37.202
Hey, guys. You look like
you're getting a little red.

00:37.204 --> 00:39.104
Maybe you ought to put
some sunblock on.

00:39.106 --> 00:40.205
Joe, we just got here.

00:40.207 --> 00:41.506
Oh, sorry about that.

00:41.508 --> 00:43.175
These got
a little mixed up.

00:43.177 --> 00:45.210
"hey, glad you guys
could make it!"

00:45.212 --> 00:47.346
Ugh, look at cleveland
over there.

00:47.348 --> 00:49.147
He's obviously cleaning his feet
in the pool

00:49.149 --> 00:52.217
Without making it look like he's
cleaning his feet in the pool.

00:52.219 --> 00:53.819
Oh, that's nice.

00:53.821 --> 00:55.387
That's a good temp.

00:55.389 --> 00:58.724
I wonder if this temp is
the same on my other foot.

00:58.726 --> 00:59.991
Oh, yeah.

00:59.993 --> 01:01.727
Sure is a good day for it.

01:01.729 --> 01:04.129
Good day for
these wet paint brushes, too.

01:04.131 --> 01:07.399
Is the pool too warm
for paint brushes?

01:10.137 --> 01:12.204
(toilet flushes)

01:12.206 --> 01:13.405
Hey, sorry again, kevin.

01:13.407 --> 01:16.375
I didn't see you in the tub.

01:29.923 --> 01:31.223
Huh, what's all this?

01:31.225 --> 01:32.557
Joe: Honey,
it doesn't seem like

01:32.559 --> 01:35.060
The griffins are leaving
anytime too soon!

01:35.062 --> 01:36.328
Oh. Hey, peter.

01:36.330 --> 01:37.996
Hey, joe. What are
all these pictures?

01:37.998 --> 01:39.398
Oh, nothing.

01:39.400 --> 01:41.333
They're just some stupid
scribbles i've been working on

01:41.335 --> 01:42.534
For a children's book.

01:42.536 --> 01:43.902
Well, i don't think
that's stupid.

01:43.904 --> 01:45.036
I think that's
awesome!

01:45.038 --> 01:46.505
I mean, my one
note on these

01:46.507 --> 01:48.573
Would be to hide a bunch
of dongs in the backgrounds,

01:48.575 --> 01:50.008
But, otherwise, i
think they're great!

01:50.010 --> 01:52.711
Wow. Well, that really means
a lot to me, peter.

01:52.713 --> 01:54.679
I've been working on this book
for nine years,

01:54.681 --> 01:56.615
But i've been too afraid
to show it to anybody.

01:56.617 --> 01:58.583
Come on, joe.
You can't be afraid.

01:58.585 --> 02:01.386
What if bono had been afraid
to wear sunglasses?

02:01.388 --> 02:02.921
Then nobody would know
about africa.

02:02.923 --> 02:04.256
What's it about?

02:04.258 --> 02:06.258
<i>Well, it's called
the hopeful squirrel.</i>

02:06.260 --> 02:07.726
It's about
a handicapped squirrel

02:07.728 --> 02:09.961
Who has to learn
to overcome his disabilities

02:09.963 --> 02:11.530
So he can survive in the wild.

02:11.532 --> 02:14.599
As you can imagine,
it's very personal to me.

02:14.601 --> 02:18.236
Wait... Were you
once a squirrel?

02:18.238 --> 02:19.905
No, peter.
I'm handicapped.

02:19.907 --> 02:22.240
Well, you know, you ought
to do something with this.

02:22.242 --> 02:23.308
Really? You think so?

02:23.310 --> 02:24.409
Hey, trust me, joe.

02:24.411 --> 02:25.744
I know talent
when i see it.

02:25.746 --> 02:27.913
I mean, i discovered
mr. Peanut.

02:27.915 --> 02:29.714
Ordinary legume.

02:29.716 --> 02:31.416
Ordinary legume.

02:31.418 --> 02:34.453
Extraordinary peanut!

02:38.225 --> 02:39.991
Oh, man.
There she is.

02:39.993 --> 02:40.959
Wha... Who?

02:40.961 --> 02:42.294
That girl,
right there.

02:42.296 --> 02:44.229
She comes in here every morning
after her run.

02:44.231 --> 02:45.764
Ah, i'm obsessed
with her.

02:45.766 --> 02:47.732
Well, why don't
you go talk to her?

02:47.734 --> 02:49.067
Way ahead of ya.

02:49.069 --> 02:50.869
Wh... Where
are you going?

02:51.338 --> 02:53.238
(panting)

02:53.240 --> 02:55.106
And... 1,000.

02:55.108 --> 02:56.174
Whew.
(laughs)

02:56.176 --> 02:57.442
1,000 what?

02:57.444 --> 02:59.411
Percent, that's what.
(scoffs)

02:59.413 --> 03:01.279
You, uh, you in
the game, too?

03:01.281 --> 03:02.681
You mean running?

03:02.683 --> 03:04.850
Uh, let me think--
what's on my trophies?

03:04.852 --> 03:06.251
Uh... Yes!

03:06.253 --> 03:07.252
Stewie:
You're losing her!

03:07.254 --> 03:08.286
Hey, i'm brian.

03:08.288 --> 03:09.287
Hi, i'm chloe.

03:09.289 --> 03:10.355
Nice to meet you.

03:10.357 --> 03:11.690
Hey, uh, you
wouldn't maybe want

03:11.692 --> 03:13.959
To grab a bite to eat
sometime, would you?

03:13.961 --> 03:14.926
That sounds great.

03:14.928 --> 03:16.027
Awesome.

03:16.029 --> 03:17.662
You know, see, this is
how you meet people.

03:17.664 --> 03:19.164
I tried the online
dating thing,

03:19.166 --> 03:21.833
But there's just too much
competition out there.

03:24.004 --> 03:26.204
Short, but handsome, slightly
hairy, newly single salesman.

03:26.206 --> 03:28.940
Short, but handsome, slightly
hairy, newly single salesman.

03:28.942 --> 03:31.643
Short, but handsome, slightly
hairy, newly single salesman.

03:31.645 --> 03:33.979
Hi, i'm al harrington
of al harrington's wacky waving

03:33.981 --> 03:36.715
Inflatable arm-flailing tube-man
warehouse and emporium.

03:36.717 --> 03:38.850
<i>Due to a gut-busting divorce,
limited people skills,</i>

03:38.852 --> 03:40.886
<i>And significant prodding
from my therapist,</i>

03:40.888 --> 03:43.288
I am currently seeking online
companionship as

03:43.290 --> 03:46.291
A short, but handsome, slightly
hairy, newly single salesman.

03:46.293 --> 03:47.726
And i would love to attempt

03:47.728 --> 03:49.828
To convert my heavily
embellished internet profile

03:49.830 --> 03:51.696
And carefully airbrushed,
out-of-date photo,

03:51.698 --> 03:56.067
Into a night of
physical intimacy with you...!

03:59.373 --> 04:00.939
(knocking)

04:03.210 --> 04:05.377
Peter, i just heard
the best news.

04:05.379 --> 04:08.046
Wow, word gets
around fast.

04:08.048 --> 04:09.047
Nice, right?

04:09.049 --> 04:10.415
No. Peter,
i took your advice

04:10.417 --> 04:12.050
And sent my book
to a publisher.

04:12.052 --> 04:14.419
<i>They're gonna publish
the hopeful squirrel.</i>

04:14.421 --> 04:15.921
And it's all
thanks to you!

04:15.923 --> 04:17.055
Joe, that's amazing!

04:17.057 --> 04:19.224
So there's gonna be a
real live book out there

04:19.226 --> 04:20.592
With your name on it?

04:20.594 --> 04:22.894
Well, actually, i'm writing it
under a pen name--

04:22.896 --> 04:24.195
David chicago.

04:24.197 --> 04:27.065
Well, how come you didn't
just write it under joe...

04:27.067 --> 04:28.400
S... Steenburj...

04:28.402 --> 04:30.068
You know,
your real name?

04:30.070 --> 04:32.504
I wanted to avoid catching crap
down at the police station.

04:32.506 --> 04:34.406
They don't like
anything artistic.

04:34.408 --> 04:36.841
They were pretty rough
on my mime act.

04:36.843 --> 04:37.776
I'm in a box.

04:37.778 --> 04:40.512
Oop, that's the
back of the box.

04:40.514 --> 04:41.913
You're not supposed
to talk!

04:41.915 --> 04:44.950
Well, how else are you
gonna know i'm in a box?!

04:47.054 --> 04:49.087
(doorbell rings)

04:49.089 --> 04:50.388
Oh. Hi, brian.

04:50.390 --> 04:51.790
Hey. You, uh...

04:51.792 --> 04:53.525
You didn't forget
about our date, did you?

04:53.527 --> 04:54.859
Of course not.

04:54.861 --> 04:56.428
I was just thinking,
since it's so nice out,

04:56.430 --> 04:58.363
We could go out for
a run and then eat.

04:58.365 --> 05:01.032
Oh. Yeah. N-no, no. You know,
i would totally do that.

05:01.034 --> 05:05.103
I-i just... I've already run,
like, so many "k" today.

05:05.105 --> 05:06.438
Oh, come on,
don't be a wimp!

05:06.440 --> 05:08.807
This way, you'll earn
your dessert.

05:08.809 --> 05:11.142
(sighs)

05:12.279 --> 05:14.579
Wow, this is great,
isn't it, brian?

05:14.581 --> 05:16.381
(panting):
Yeah, it's awesome.

05:16.383 --> 05:18.316
Hey, uh, is your vision

05:18.318 --> 05:20.619
Also reduced
to just a tiny pinhole?

05:20.621 --> 05:22.220
Just push
through it, brian.

05:22.222 --> 05:23.755
Once you hit
your runner's high,

05:23.757 --> 05:25.423
You'll catch
your second wind.

05:25.425 --> 05:26.625
Runner's high?

05:26.627 --> 05:28.560
Yeah, my endorphins
always kick in

05:28.562 --> 05:30.629
At the top of this hill.

05:31.898 --> 05:33.298
Oh, crap.

05:33.300 --> 05:35.700
(panting)

05:37.838 --> 05:39.671
<i>Brian, this is your heart.</i>

05:39.673 --> 05:41.239
<i>What the hell do you think
you're doing?</i>

05:41.241 --> 05:42.407
<i>Stop.</i>

05:42.409 --> 05:44.142
<i>Brian, this is your penis.</i>

05:44.144 --> 05:45.243
<i>Don't listen to him.</i>

05:45.245 --> 05:46.678
<i>We're this close to bone city.</i>

05:46.680 --> 05:48.747
<i>Peter:
Brian, i'm here, too.</i>

05:48.749 --> 05:51.483
<i>I'm hanging out with your penis
and your heart.</i>

05:51.485 --> 05:53.585
Okay, here comes the top.

05:53.587 --> 05:55.153
Chloe, i'm not sure i can...

05:55.155 --> 05:57.122
♪ ♪

05:57.124 --> 05:59.424
I feel it.

05:59.426 --> 06:01.693
I'm feeling the runner's high.

06:01.695 --> 06:04.529
♪ it was a beautiful day ♪

06:04.531 --> 06:06.865
♪ the sun beat down ♪

06:06.867 --> 06:08.533
♪ i had the radio on... ♪

06:08.535 --> 06:11.036
Go get 'em, brian!
(chuckles)

06:11.038 --> 06:14.305
By the way, the sun
is really a black guy.

06:14.307 --> 06:16.508
The moon is korean!

06:16.510 --> 06:18.710
Wow, this is amazing.

06:18.712 --> 06:21.546
I never want to lose
this feeling.

06:21.548 --> 06:24.549
♪ yeah, i'm running'
down a dream ♪

06:24.551 --> 06:27.385
♪ that never would come to me ♪

06:27.387 --> 06:31.222
♪ workin' on a mystery... ♪

06:32.059 --> 06:33.324
Oh, brian.

06:33.326 --> 06:34.726
That was incredible.

06:34.728 --> 06:37.962
Yeah, you hump her
real good, brian!

06:37.964 --> 06:40.432
I'm gonna go ahead
and close the shades.

06:41.201 --> 06:44.102
I still see you!

06:46.873 --> 06:48.339
Hello, everyone.
I'm blake walker

06:48.341 --> 06:49.708
From piermont publishing.

06:49.710 --> 06:52.544
Please join me in welcoming
david chicago.

06:52.546 --> 06:54.212
(applause)

06:54.214 --> 06:57.716
Okay, so, uh, hi, folks,
and thank you all for coming.

06:57.718 --> 07:00.251
I know this would've been
a great day to surf.

07:00.253 --> 07:01.720
Peter:
That's not a joke!

07:01.722 --> 07:05.090
<i>Uh, anyway,
this is the hopeful squirrel.</i>

07:05.092 --> 07:07.659
"there once was
a handicapped squirrel

07:07.661 --> 07:10.228
Who could not climb trees
to get food."

07:10.230 --> 07:12.430
Okay, next page.

07:16.403 --> 07:17.702
"the squirrel"--

07:17.704 --> 07:19.404
The same squirrel
from the first page--

07:19.406 --> 07:22.607
"hoped that the other animals
would share their food with him.

07:22.609 --> 07:24.676
"'please,'
said the hopeful squirrel.

07:24.678 --> 07:26.878
"'if you could all spare
just one nut,

07:26.880 --> 07:29.280
I, too, could survive
the winter.'"

07:29.282 --> 07:30.715
Sorry about that.

07:30.717 --> 07:33.017
Mommy, i don't like
the wheel man.

07:33.019 --> 07:34.786
"but none of the other animals

07:34.788 --> 07:38.289
Would share
with the hopeful squirrel."

07:38.291 --> 07:39.924
Hey, eyes front! I'm talking!

07:39.926 --> 07:41.559
Don't tell my kid what to do.

07:41.561 --> 07:43.595
Well, maybe if you did,
i wouldn't have to!

07:43.597 --> 07:45.430
(parents grumbling)

07:45.432 --> 07:46.865
Shut up! This is free!

07:46.867 --> 07:48.066
Quagmire:
You know why it's free?

07:48.068 --> 07:49.968
'cause it sucks!
Quagmire?

07:49.970 --> 07:52.971
I think it might
be time to leave.

07:52.973 --> 07:55.240
Ah, crap, this is joe's dream.

07:55.242 --> 07:56.808
I got to do something.

07:56.810 --> 07:58.243
Joe, what are
you doing?

07:58.245 --> 08:00.278
The-the squirrel doesn't
even sound hopeful.

08:00.280 --> 08:01.579
It's got to be like,

08:01.581 --> 08:03.615
(cheerfully): "if you
could spare just one nut,

08:03.617 --> 08:05.917
I, too, could
survive the winter!"

08:05.919 --> 08:07.485
Oh, i like that voice.

08:07.487 --> 08:08.920
He's funny.

08:08.922 --> 08:10.822
That's the man who passed out
at the liquor store.

08:10.824 --> 08:12.957
Joe, quick,
give me the book.

08:12.959 --> 08:17.095
"and so, the squirrel decided
to climb for his own nuts.

08:17.097 --> 08:20.231
"'i don't need legs when
i've got a positive attitude

08:20.233 --> 08:22.133
And arm strength.'"

08:22.135 --> 08:24.936
"'i'm sorry that
we mistreated you,'

08:24.938 --> 08:26.805
"said buddy the badger.

08:26.807 --> 08:28.473
"'could you find it
in your heart

08:28.475 --> 08:29.908
"to share your nuts with us?'

08:29.910 --> 08:32.443
"'of course i'll share
with you all,'

08:32.445 --> 08:33.678
"said the squirrel.

08:33.680 --> 08:35.180
"'for if i could not forgive,

08:35.182 --> 08:38.516
Then i would be
truly handicapped.'"

08:38.518 --> 08:40.051
(cheering)

08:45.592 --> 08:47.759
Wow, that was great.
Who are you?

08:47.761 --> 08:50.128
Just a grown man
with a pet hermit crab.

08:50.130 --> 08:52.530
Listen, joe, how would you feel
about your friend

08:52.532 --> 08:54.432
Getting more involved?
What do you mean?

08:54.434 --> 08:56.968
Well, you would write the books,
and your friend, peter,

08:56.970 --> 08:59.304
<i>Would be the public face
of the hopeful squirrel.</i>

08:59.306 --> 09:00.772
He would be david chicago.

09:00.774 --> 09:03.608
Well, i...
I don't know.

09:03.610 --> 09:05.109
Joe, this happens
all the time.

09:05.111 --> 09:06.644
You wouldn't believe
who really writes

09:06.646 --> 09:08.213
All those stephen king books.

09:08.215 --> 09:10.782
Scary stuff, scary stuff,
scary stuff. Ding!

09:10.784 --> 09:13.051
Scary stuff,
scary stuff, scary stuff. Ding!

09:13.053 --> 09:16.054
Scary stuff, scary stuff,
scary stuff. Lunch!

09:16.056 --> 09:18.489
Look, peter can get this book
into the hands

09:18.491 --> 09:19.891
Of every kid in america.

09:19.893 --> 09:21.392
That's what you wanted,
isn't it?

09:21.394 --> 09:22.827
All right.

09:22.829 --> 09:25.396
Well, whatever you think
is best for the book.

09:25.398 --> 09:27.131
Great! So it's all agreed.

09:27.133 --> 09:29.234
Can't wait to work
with you, peter.

09:29.236 --> 09:31.369
What-what just happened?

09:31.371 --> 09:33.805
Oh, the bookstore closed
and is now a target.

09:33.807 --> 09:36.941
But don't worry,
our industry's fine.

09:42.716 --> 09:44.716
Excuse me, mr. Chicago?

09:44.718 --> 09:46.551
Could you please sign
my copy of your book?

09:46.553 --> 09:48.152
Sure, i...
Easy there, joe.

09:48.154 --> 09:50.555
Hot rod asked for mr. Chicago.

09:52.392 --> 09:55.059
"give me all your money.
I have a gun"?

09:55.061 --> 09:57.729
Oh, wait, i think
i messed something up.

09:57.731 --> 10:00.265
"never give up on your dreams"?

10:02.402 --> 10:04.669
Listen, peter, if you're
gonna act as david chicago,

10:04.671 --> 10:07.171
I need to know that you're
gonna take this seriously

10:07.173 --> 10:09.374
And honor the message
of the book.

10:09.376 --> 10:10.942
Joe, i got it. Trust me.

10:10.944 --> 10:12.176
This ain't the first time

10:12.178 --> 10:14.078
I've pretended
to be someone i'm not.

10:14.080 --> 10:15.947
(making ghost noises)

10:15.949 --> 10:19.450
Gene shalit, i am the
ghost of roger ebert.

10:19.452 --> 10:21.119
(screams)
and even in death,

10:21.121 --> 10:23.021
I'm a better
critic than you.

10:23.023 --> 10:25.223
Leave me alone!
Go back to hell!

10:25.225 --> 10:26.090
(hisses)

10:26.092 --> 10:28.526
Gene, is everything
all right?

10:28.528 --> 10:29.594
It's fine, joanne.

10:29.596 --> 10:31.296
Go back to sleep.

10:32.632 --> 10:35.033
(kissing noisily)

10:37.704 --> 10:39.470
(grunts, snorts)

10:44.044 --> 10:45.576
Good afternoon,
i'm tom tucker.

10:45.578 --> 10:48.746
<i>Welcome to another edition
of cross-legged chat.</i>

10:48.748 --> 10:50.315
Our guest on
today's show is

10:50.317 --> 10:53.718
Local bestselling children's
book author david chicago.

10:53.720 --> 10:55.086
Welcome.
Thank you.

10:55.088 --> 10:57.422
Wow, all your words are
right there for you?

10:57.424 --> 10:58.456
(laughs)

10:58.458 --> 11:00.792
Quite... Quite the imagination
on this one.

11:00.794 --> 11:02.460
So, tell me,
how did you decide

11:02.462 --> 11:05.029
To write about
a handicapped squirrel?

11:05.932 --> 11:07.265
You know, i'd see
these crippled kids

11:07.267 --> 11:09.267
Limping down the sidewalk
on my way to work,

11:09.269 --> 11:11.302
And i would just
laugh and laugh,

11:11.304 --> 11:13.504
And i thought,
"hey! Put that in a book!"

11:13.506 --> 11:15.173
(laughter)

11:15.175 --> 11:18.643
He's making people laugh
at handicapped people.

11:18.645 --> 11:19.811
What's he doing out there?!

11:19.813 --> 11:21.079
I'll tell you
what he's doing,

11:21.081 --> 11:22.413
He's selling books!
They love him!

11:22.415 --> 11:24.515
Now, i understand
we have some questions

11:24.517 --> 11:25.583
From the audience.

11:25.585 --> 11:26.951
Yes, i have a question.

11:26.953 --> 11:29.287
Is the hopeful squirrel
a boy or a girl?

11:29.289 --> 11:30.922
(high-pitched voice):
I'm a boy!

11:30.924 --> 11:33.024
But in the book,
i'm drawn smooth down there,

11:33.026 --> 11:35.093
So it's not a bad question.

11:35.095 --> 11:36.527
Okay, that's all our time.

11:36.529 --> 11:38.329
We invite you to stay tuned
through the credits

11:38.331 --> 11:40.698
So you can see
where i buy my clothes.

11:40.700 --> 11:43.935
(cheering, music playing)

11:52.612 --> 11:53.978
So what's
going on here?

11:53.980 --> 11:55.279
Just having dinner.

11:55.281 --> 11:57.715
That's dad's chair.
He's gonna be mad.

11:57.717 --> 12:01.185
Wow, brian, you sure have been
doing a lot of jogging lately.

12:01.187 --> 12:03.354
(chuckles)
it's called "running," lois.

12:03.356 --> 12:04.889
Why don't you
have some food?

12:04.891 --> 12:06.324
Oh, you mean fuel?

12:06.326 --> 12:08.493
Ah, no-no offense,
lois, but that stuff

12:08.495 --> 12:10.228
Is nothing but chemicals
and empty calories.

12:10.230 --> 12:13.131
Okay. I'll mush some up
and put it on the floor

12:13.133 --> 12:15.033
Next to the trash,
if you get hungry.

12:15.035 --> 12:17.035
I think you bought
girl running shoes.

12:17.037 --> 12:18.736
You know, in case
any of you want to,

12:18.738 --> 12:20.004
Uh, come cheer us on,

12:20.006 --> 12:21.973
Chloe and i are doing
the quahog marathon

12:21.975 --> 12:23.007
In a couple weeks.

12:23.009 --> 12:24.475
A marathon?

12:24.477 --> 12:26.544
But-but what if that sexy boy
has another bomb?

12:26.546 --> 12:29.147
Yeah, are you sure
you can finish a marathon?

12:29.149 --> 12:30.381
I'm not worried, meg.

12:30.383 --> 12:32.083
I'm just gonna give it
all i've got,

12:32.085 --> 12:34.685
<i>Like scotty
engineering the enterprise.</i>

12:34.687 --> 12:36.020
(alarm blaring)

12:36.022 --> 12:37.388
Scotty, we need more speed!

12:37.390 --> 12:39.557
Scotty: I'm giving her
all she's got, captain!

12:39.559 --> 12:40.992
She can't take any more!

12:40.994 --> 12:43.661
Damn. Chekov, reroute
auxiliary power to the helm.

12:43.663 --> 12:45.263
Scotty to the bridge.

12:45.265 --> 12:48.332
Uh... Captain, this is, uh...
This is a little embarrassing,

12:48.334 --> 12:50.234
But, uh, you know,
i've never noticed, uh,

12:50.236 --> 12:52.236
The little lever
i've been pushing, it's...

12:52.238 --> 12:54.338
It's only about two-thirds
of the way up.

12:54.340 --> 12:56.207
I-i actually can give her more.

12:56.209 --> 12:57.375
That's great, scotty!

12:57.377 --> 12:58.743
Mr. Spock, give us
readings on...

12:58.745 --> 13:00.378
Scotty:
Uh, c-captain, scotty again.

13:00.380 --> 13:02.180
Y... You're not gonna
believe this.

13:02.182 --> 13:04.182
Uh, there is another
lever here, too.

13:04.184 --> 13:07.085
The ship can literally go
three times as fast.

13:07.087 --> 13:08.519
I... (laughs)
i'm sorry.

13:08.521 --> 13:10.888
I feel like such a capital-j
jerk right now.

13:10.890 --> 13:12.190
It's okay, scotty.

13:12.192 --> 13:13.958
Lieutenant uhura,
open all channels for...

13:13.960 --> 13:16.761
Captain, i've-i've got to, uh,
interrupt again.

13:16.763 --> 13:18.129
I've just been thinking about

13:18.131 --> 13:19.630
This-this "giving her
all she's got" thing.

13:19.632 --> 13:22.733
I mean, i've been completely
wrong for years now.

13:22.735 --> 13:24.102
I-i feel terrible.

13:24.104 --> 13:26.137
I mean, think of how many
crises we've been in

13:26.139 --> 13:28.306
Where the issue was
how fast we could go.

13:28.308 --> 13:30.741
I-i mean... I'm sorry, captain.

13:30.743 --> 13:31.909
Scotty, it's okay.

13:31.911 --> 13:32.944
No, it's not!

13:32.946 --> 13:34.545
Eric's dead!

13:34.547 --> 13:37.115
At the funeral, i literally
said the words to his wife,

13:37.117 --> 13:38.816
"i was giving her
all she's got."

13:38.818 --> 13:40.118
Scotty, it's fine.

13:40.120 --> 13:41.319
Sulu, lock phasers...

13:41.321 --> 13:42.887
Captain, i just
got to jump in here.

13:42.889 --> 13:44.589
W-we don't have enough
dilithium crystals

13:44.591 --> 13:46.290
To run the phasers.

13:47.227 --> 13:50.695
I've-i've lost all credibility,
haven't i?

13:54.300 --> 13:56.834
Peter, i think
we need to talk.

13:56.836 --> 13:58.302
You totally screwed up my book.

13:58.304 --> 14:00.738
You're getting kids to laugh
at handicapped people,

14:00.740 --> 14:02.340
When i'm trying to inspire them.

14:02.342 --> 14:04.509
I'm afraid you're
off the project.

14:04.511 --> 14:05.409
What?

14:05.411 --> 14:06.911
You can't kick me
off the project.

14:06.913 --> 14:08.012
I'm david chicago!

14:08.014 --> 14:09.413
I'm the one who
wrote the book.

14:09.415 --> 14:11.149
Joe, come on.
Let's not kid ourselves.

14:11.151 --> 14:12.650
All right?
Everybody knows my face now.

14:12.652 --> 14:14.752
And besides, i'm the only
one of the two of us

14:14.754 --> 14:16.487
Who can do
a squirrel voice.

14:16.489 --> 14:18.256
(high-pitched voice):
Well, i don't know
if that's quite true.

14:18.258 --> 14:20.191
Joe, joe, stop.
You're embarrassing yourself.

14:20.193 --> 14:22.827
Sorry, joe, but
the publisher loves me.

14:22.829 --> 14:24.162
The public loves me.

14:24.164 --> 14:25.296
I'm not going anywhere.

14:25.298 --> 14:26.831
Screw you, peter!
You know what?

14:26.833 --> 14:28.032
You've ruined this for me.

14:28.034 --> 14:29.834
I want nothing
to do with the book,

14:29.836 --> 14:31.836
And i want nothing
to do with you!

14:33.473 --> 14:37.275
Aw, one of his shoes fell off
during the anger.

14:42.715 --> 14:44.615
(toilet flushes, door opens)

14:44.617 --> 14:47.518
Peter, bonnie told me
that joe's very upset.

14:47.520 --> 14:49.554
Did you really take
his book away from him?

14:49.556 --> 14:51.689
Did you just poop
and then get into bed

14:51.691 --> 14:52.657
Without underwear on?

14:52.659 --> 14:54.559
That book really
meant a lot to joe.

14:54.561 --> 14:56.227
I think you should
talk to him.

14:56.229 --> 14:58.362
Hey, that book would've
been nothing without me.

14:58.364 --> 15:00.231
And besides,
he's the one who quit.

15:00.233 --> 15:02.033
Now the publisher
wants another book

15:02.035 --> 15:03.234
And it's all on me!

15:03.236 --> 15:05.336
I just hate to see
you two in a fight.

15:05.338 --> 15:08.206
And on the same week
when my sister and i

15:08.208 --> 15:10.741
Are having such
a big fight, too.

15:12.212 --> 15:13.945
Good night, lois.

15:18.017 --> 15:19.917
All right, guys.
Ideas, ideas.

15:19.919 --> 15:21.552
We got a hopeful squirrel
book to write.

15:21.554 --> 15:23.054
All right, now,
who's got something?

15:23.056 --> 15:24.522
I-i got... I got something.

15:24.524 --> 15:28.926
What if the squirrel
has lasers...

15:28.928 --> 15:30.695
That he shoots
out of his eyes!

15:30.697 --> 15:31.696
Quagmire's
on the board.

15:31.698 --> 15:34.098
And how 'bout
he got a frog friend

15:34.100 --> 15:35.766
That's got some sort
of catchphrase?

15:35.768 --> 15:38.603
Like, if he's seeing something
kooky, he could be like,

15:38.605 --> 15:42.540
"damn, that's cray-cray
in a good way, right there!"

15:42.542 --> 15:43.608
Wow.

15:43.610 --> 15:45.376
God just speaks
right through you,

15:45.378 --> 15:46.377
Doesn't he, cleveland?

15:46.379 --> 15:47.712
I believe he does.

15:47.714 --> 15:48.879
Okay, what else,
what else?

15:48.881 --> 15:51.382
If there's
a bison...

15:51.384 --> 15:53.084
Is that a statement
or a question?

15:53.086 --> 15:54.352
It is what it is.

15:54.354 --> 15:56.787
Ain't nothing gotta
be nothing, huh?

15:59.892 --> 16:02.727
Brian: Hey, stewie! Can you come
in the bathroom for a second?

16:02.729 --> 16:03.928
(sighs)

16:03.930 --> 16:06.063
What is it, bri...
Oh, my god!

16:06.065 --> 16:07.598
Hey, could you
close the gate?

16:07.600 --> 16:10.735
Couple of calves
got loose. Ha, pow!

16:10.737 --> 16:12.270
Brian, you're all sinewy.

16:12.272 --> 16:14.972
Your whole body looks like
paul mccartney's neck.

16:14.974 --> 16:16.907
Thanks.
That's not
a compliment.

16:16.909 --> 16:18.109
You look terrible.

16:18.111 --> 16:19.477
What does your
girlfriend think of this?

16:19.479 --> 16:21.078
I dumped her; she
couldn't keep up with me.

16:21.080 --> 16:22.580
Hey, grab me some more
band-aids, will you?

16:22.582 --> 16:23.914
I got, like, eight
more nipples

16:23.916 --> 16:25.483
To cover up
before my run.

16:25.485 --> 16:29.120
You know, whatever you're doing,
it isn't healthy, brian.

16:29.122 --> 16:30.554
Oh, i'm not healthy?

16:30.556 --> 16:33.057
Stewie, my heart rate is
down to four beats a minute.

16:33.059 --> 16:34.558
Besides, i got
to keep training.

16:34.560 --> 16:36.294
The marathon's
in two days.

16:36.296 --> 16:39.163
Brian, i-i'm worried you're
losing yourself in all this.

16:39.165 --> 16:40.564
Do you remember that phase

16:40.566 --> 16:42.466
When you thought
you were a pointer dog?

16:42.468 --> 16:45.403
Was someone wearing
my new high heels?

16:46.572 --> 16:48.339
You dick.

16:55.081 --> 16:57.315
(dramatic music playing)

16:57.317 --> 16:59.083
Quagmire (over p.A. System):
Ladies and gentlemen,

16:59.085 --> 17:00.418
Boys and girls,

17:00.420 --> 17:02.853
Hot moms who are married
but looking...

17:03.656 --> 17:06.257
David chicago!

17:06.259 --> 17:08.793
(crowd cheering)

17:08.795 --> 17:12.163
Hey, how many of
y'all bitches like to read?

17:12.165 --> 17:14.732
(cheering)

17:16.202 --> 17:17.535
"chapter one.

17:17.537 --> 17:19.303
"it was winter in the forest,

17:19.305 --> 17:22.473
"so the squirrel was happy
he'd built that hot tub.

17:22.475 --> 17:26.177
"but little did he know,
a strain of super gonorrhea

17:26.179 --> 17:27.678
"was gonna hit him so fierce

17:27.680 --> 17:31.182
"he'd wish he was still
paralyzed from the waist down.

17:31.184 --> 17:33.818
"on top of that,
some son of a bitch

17:33.820 --> 17:35.720
Killed his brother."

17:37.123 --> 17:38.989
"the monkey's
kick-ass buzz saw hand

17:38.991 --> 17:40.391
"tore his head open.

17:40.393 --> 17:43.494
"'his brains, his brains--
they're everywhere!'

17:43.496 --> 17:45.196
The little girl yelled."

17:45.198 --> 17:47.665
Cleveland:
"'damn, that's cray-cray
in a good way, right there!'"

17:47.667 --> 17:49.967
"...Exclaimed
billy the bullfrog."

17:49.969 --> 17:53.304
"the woodchuck mom and her baby
finished their cocoa

17:53.306 --> 17:56.040
"and then tucked in
for another cozy night.

17:56.042 --> 17:58.042
But then..."

17:58.044 --> 18:01.312
"'nothing but cops on the take
and hookers on the make,'

18:01.314 --> 18:02.713
"said randy the raccoon.

18:02.715 --> 18:05.883
"'what's a hooker?'
asked the bunny, who was gay.

18:05.885 --> 18:07.051
"'that and a bag of crank

18:07.053 --> 18:09.220
"is my saturday night!'
spat randy.

18:09.222 --> 18:11.789
The end."

18:12.592 --> 18:14.492
You're awful.
That was the worst.

18:14.494 --> 18:16.627
We had trouble hearing
you in the back.

18:19.065 --> 18:22.366
I'm sorry, peter,
you're fired.

18:22.368 --> 18:25.569
I'm sorry joe's dream
didn't work out for you, peter.

18:25.571 --> 18:27.605
(sighs)
what was i thinking?

18:27.607 --> 18:30.007
Joe's the one with
all the talent.

18:30.009 --> 18:31.375
Me trying to
write a book

18:31.377 --> 18:34.044
Is like ceelo trying to
find a pair of pants.

18:34.046 --> 18:38.482
Yeah, i need to find something
a cartoon apple would wear.

18:42.555 --> 18:43.854
Hey, you made it!

18:43.856 --> 18:45.790
So you ready to watch
me kick some ass?

18:45.792 --> 18:47.925
Brian, i think you've taken
all of this too far.

18:47.927 --> 18:50.528
You know, there is such a thing
as too much exercise.

18:50.530 --> 18:52.296
Stewie, i know you're
worried, all right?

18:52.298 --> 18:54.231
And no offense, but
i'm not taking advice

18:54.233 --> 18:55.599
From a guy
who eats bread.

18:55.601 --> 18:57.701
Announcer:
Runners, take your marks!

19:05.812 --> 19:08.312
(screams)
oh, son of a bitch!

19:08.314 --> 19:09.914
Ow, my leg!

19:09.916 --> 19:11.382
Help me, somebody!

19:11.384 --> 19:13.784
(grunting, groaning)

19:17.890 --> 19:22.193
Brian, why does everything
you touch turn to garbage?

19:29.001 --> 19:30.067
Peter.

19:30.069 --> 19:32.102
Look, joe,
i messed up.

19:32.104 --> 19:33.637
All right? I just...

19:33.639 --> 19:36.674
I just got so wrapped up
in all the attention.

19:36.676 --> 19:39.343
The attention
you deserved.

19:39.345 --> 19:40.945
I know how much
this meant to you,

19:40.947 --> 19:43.514
And i... I should've
just stayed out of it.

19:43.516 --> 19:45.483
Listen, i'm...

19:45.485 --> 19:48.352
I'm sorry
i mistreated you.

19:48.354 --> 19:51.121
Okay?
You deserve better.

19:51.123 --> 19:52.456
Peter, wait.

19:52.458 --> 19:54.692
If i could
not forgive,

19:54.694 --> 19:57.127
Then i would be
truly handicapped.

19:57.129 --> 19:58.128
What?

19:58.130 --> 19:59.363
It's from the
book, peter.

19:59.365 --> 20:00.331
What book?

20:00.333 --> 20:01.665
I forgive you, peter.

20:01.667 --> 20:02.633
You do?

20:02.635 --> 20:04.268
Yeah.
The truth is, without you,

20:04.270 --> 20:05.936
I never would have
had the confidence

20:05.938 --> 20:08.105
To get my book published
in the first place.

20:08.107 --> 20:09.974
And that's all i ever wanted.

20:09.976 --> 20:11.442
Friends?

20:11.444 --> 20:13.744
Frasier.

20:18.150 --> 20:19.483
So, bri, how's
that ankle itch?

20:19.485 --> 20:20.651
Well, what
do you mean?

20:20.653 --> 20:21.819
I'm just saying,
you probably have

20:21.821 --> 20:23.487
An itchy ankle
under that cast.

20:23.489 --> 20:24.655
It starts as a tickle

20:24.657 --> 20:26.023
And then you can't
quite reach it?

20:26.025 --> 20:27.658
Not gonna work,
stewie.
Yes, you're right.

20:27.660 --> 20:28.826
Best not
to think about it.

20:28.828 --> 20:30.528
Even though it might
be a little bug

20:30.530 --> 20:32.296
Digging away
down there,

20:32.298 --> 20:33.731
Just nagging
and itching and...

20:33.733 --> 20:35.866
Ah, ah, crap,
i did it to myself!

20:35.868 --> 20:37.401
Ah, what is that?

20:37.403 --> 20:40.137
Well, peter, i'm glad
you made up with joe.

20:40.139 --> 20:41.372
Yeah, me, too.

20:41.374 --> 20:43.240
It just goes
to show you, lois,

20:43.242 --> 20:44.875
Books is bad news.

20:44.877 --> 20:47.344
Well, except for the books
they sell at urban outfitters.

20:47.346 --> 20:49.914
<i>The single girls'
guide to happy hour.</i>

20:49.916 --> 20:52.149
<i>Dogs who look
like presidents.</i>

20:52.151 --> 20:55.586
This one's just pictures
of people reacting to farts.

20:55.588 --> 20:58.756
I like where
the usa is headed.

20:58.757 --> 20:59.757
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru